    "m2_prompt_trader_proposal_original": "**Action**: Hold\n\n**Reasoning**: The investment plan presents a genuinely balanced case for AMZN. The long-term structural trend is clearly constructive: price sits 15.3% above the rising 200-day SMA ($159.35), the 50-day SMA is rising, and fundamentals are strong with $18.99B in Q1 operating cash flow and a 41% equity-to-asset ratio. However, the short-term setup is unconfirmed \u2014 price sits marginally below the 10-EMA ($184.07), the 5-day return is negative, the 20-day return is flat, relative volume is 25% below average at 0.75, and RSI is neutral at 51. The MACD bullish crossover occurred only three days ago without a confirmed breakout through resistance at $188.50. Given the unconfirmed short-term setup and meaningful data gaps (no news, sentiment, or macro data available), the prudent stance is to maintain existing positions without aggressive entry. Confirmation triggers are clear: a daily close above $188.50 on above-average volume would justify adding, while a close below $176.44 would warrant trimming. For any new tranche, a stop-loss at $176.50 with moderate sizing (~2x ATR stop distance) is appropriate given gap risk.\n\n**Entry Price**: 183.66\n\n**Stop Loss**: 176.5\n\n**Position Sizing**: Maintain existing positions; for new capital, starter position of one-third to one-half of intended size, with remainder deployed only on bullish confirmation (close above $188.50 on volume >1.0). Moderate sizing given ~2x ATR stop distance.\n\nFINAL TRANSACTION PROPOSAL: **HOLD**",
